// so i think it better to change the way we store the types in general so first
// blocks
// block and machine will only take a return type and if it don't have one will be take all (block or machine) scopes
// so name<block> // will take any block regard of the return type same with machine
// to set a return type name<block<<return type>>> ex : name<block<int32>>
// micro and method and lambda and fn 
// will be name<<block type><(<params types>),<return type>>> ex :  name<fn<(int32,int32),int32>>
// but when it be name<<block type>>
// with no set <(<params types>),<return type>> it will take a block typed scope regard of other types (par ty,ret ty)
// and for name<<block type>><(<params types>)> it will take a block typed (with the set params) scope regard of other types (ret ty)
// and for name<<block type>><<return type>> it will take a block typed (with the set return) scope regard of other types (par ty)
